  ('1068250502394501349', 'The Windermere Children', 2020, 'Drama, War, History', 'Michael Samuels', 'Simon Block', 'Thomas Kretschmann, Romola Garai, Iain Glen, Tim McInnerny, Marcel Sabat, Philipp Christopher, Anna Schumacher, Konstantin Frank', 'NR', 'The story of the pioneering project to rehabilitate child survivors of the Holocaust on the shores of Lake Windermere.', 'The story of the pioneering project to rehabilitate child survivors of the Holocaust on the shores of Lake Windermere.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/4RnQMwVVxhJlZDJybptAOrrpt87.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:664423'),
  ('634960290675349979', 'The Windmill', 1986, 'Comedy, History', 'Recep Biçer, Atıf Yılmaz, Orhan Oğuz', 'Barış Pirhasan', 'Şener Şen, Serap Aksoy, Ali Erkazan, Orhan Çağman, Taner Barlas, Oktay Sözbir, Kemal İnci, Nuri Tuğ', null, 'In the last years of the Ottoman Empire, a poor little Anatolian town named Saripinar is hit by a minor earthquake which has neither destroyed nor left it with many casualties. However, a telegraph sent to the central government exaggerates the situation and mentions that the governor of the town has been severely wounded, making the event a nationwide matter.', 'In the last years of the Ottoman Empire, a poor little Anatolian town named Saripinar is hit by a minor earthquake which has neither destroyed nor left it with many casualties. However, a telegraph sent to the central government exaggerates the situation and mentions that the governor of the town has been severely wounded, making the event a nationwide matter.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/4N3qikpEcTBLooR86hx6PAfMLmX.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:232326'),
  ('787868138288041257', 'The Windmill Massacre', 2016, 'Drama, Horror', 'Nick Jongerius, Bart Beekman, Suzanne Andriessen', 'Chris W. Mitchell, Suzy Quid', 'Patrick Baladi, Ben Batt, Charlotte Beaumont, Fiona Hampton, Tanroh Ishida, Bart Klever, Kenan Raven, Noah Taylor', null, 'Jennifer, an Australian girl on the run from her past, turns up in Amsterdam and, in a desperate attempt to blend in, joins a coach-load of tourists on a tour of Holland''s old windmills. When the bus breaks down in the middle of nowhere, she and the other tourists are forced to seek shelter in a disused shed beside a sinister windmill where a devil-worshiping miller once ground the bones of locals instead of grain. As members of the group start to disappear, Jennifer learns that they all have something in common – a shared secret that seems to mark them all for doom.', 'Jennifer, an Australian girl on the run from her past, turns up in Amsterdam and, in a desperate attempt to blend in, joins a coach-load of tourists on a tour of Holland''s old windmills. When the bus breaks down in the middle of nowhere, she and the other tourists are forced to seek shelter in a disused shed beside a sinister windmill where a devil-worshiping miller once ground the bones of locals instead of grain. As members of the group start to disappear, Jennifer learns that they all have something in common – a shared secret that seems to mark them all for doom.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/jlmbMnrzxkFaSa8UnHefY4tNuOp.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:397514'),
  ('333114984749168736', 'The Window', 1949, 'Thriller, Crime', 'Ted Tetzlaff, Robert De Grasse, William O. Steiner', 'Mel Dinelli', 'Bobby Driscoll, Barbara Hale, Arthur Kennedy, Paul Stewart, Ruth Roman, Richard Benedict, James Nolan, Anthony Ross', null, 'An imaginative boy who frequently makes things up witnesses a murder, but can''t get his parents or the police to believe him. The only people taking him seriously are the killers - who live upstairs, know that he saw what they did, and are out to permanently silence him.', 'An imaginative boy who frequently makes things up witnesses a murder, but can''t get his parents or the police to believe him. The only people taking him seriously are the killers - who live upstairs, know that he saw what they did, and are out to permanently silence him.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/pez60cVCRjy2os36iI4YXYWTrRT.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:32684'),
  ('161502493663769203', 'The Window', 2009, 'Drama', 'Carlos Sorin', 'Carlos Sorin', 'Antonio Larreta, María del Carmen Jiménez, Emilse Roldán, Roberto Rovira, Carla Peterson', null, 'It is a significant day for 80 year old Antonio. After an absence of many years, his estranged son is coming to visit. All must be perfect. There will be a toast with a very special champagne an embrace; warm words that may finally bridge the gap between them-- But before, Antonio must wait. Bedridden, he looks out his window at the Patagonian landscape and sees light and life, the past and the pr', 'It is a significant day for 80 year old Antonio. After an absence of many years, his estranged son is coming to visit. All must be perfect. There will be a toast with a very special champagne an embrace; warm words that may finally bridge the gap between them-- But before, Antonio must wait. Bedridden, he looks out his window at the Patagonian landscape and sees light and life, the past and the pr', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/gyrzh7929zwHVR1PBkDvlAQywRb.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:21409'),
  ('560725407767712170', 'The Windshield Wiper', 2021, 'Animation, Romance', 'Marco Regina, Alberto Mielgo', 'Alberto Mielgo', 'Kara Whitfield, Fanny Rosen, Charlie Bean, Jake Bercovici, Zachary Rosencrantz, Anka Tiribeja, Alberto Mielgo, John Duffin', null, 'Inside a cafe while smoking a whole pack of cigarettes, a man poses an ambitious question: "What is Love?". A collection of vignettes and situations will lead the man to the desired conclusion.', 'Inside a cafe while smoking a whole pack of cigarettes, a man poses an ambitious question: "What is Love?". A collection of vignettes and situations will lead the man to the desired conclusion.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/hkfe9DfheH7zRu8Yj2wXqukbrTx.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:601329'),
  ('923965570998543471', 'The Wing or the Thigh?', 1976, 'Comedy', 'Claude Zidi, Wladimir Ivanov, Claude Renoir', 'Michel Fabre, Claude Zidi', 'Louis de Funès, Coluche, Ann Zacharias, Julien Guiomar, Raymond Bussières, Philippe Bouvard, Daniel Langlet, Claude Gensac', null, 'Charles Duchemin, a well-known gourmet and publisher of a famous restaurant guide, is waging a war against fast food entrepreneur Tri- catel to save the French art of cooking. After having agreed to appear on a talk show to show his skills in naming food and wine by taste, he is confronted with two disasters: his son wants to become a clown rather than a restaurant tester and he, the famous Charles Duchemin, has lost his taste!', 'Charles Duchemin, a well-known gourmet and publisher of a famous restaurant guide, is waging a war against fast food entrepreneur Tri- catel to save the French art of cooking. After having agreed to appear on a talk show to show his skills in naming food and wine by taste, he is confronted with two disasters: his son wants to become a clown rather than a restaurant tester and he, the famous Charles Duchemin, has lost his taste!', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/h9lEYJ6tuglAWjaiYDHoUMsBh0X.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:761'),
