  ('295544552405050644', 'This Is Me…Now', 2024, 'Drama, Music, Documentary', 'Dave Meyers, Andrew Coffing, Daniela Giraldo', 'Matt Walton, Jennifer Lopez', 'Jennifer Lopez, Ben Affleck, Idaliz Christian, Fat Joe, Matthew Law, Brandon Delsid, Alix Angelis, Malcolm Kelner', 'PG-13', 'An intimate, fantastical and narrative-driven reflection of Jennifer Lopez''s journey of self-healing and self-love in an immersive world where music and visuals intertwine, revealing the challenges faced and the triumphs achieved.', 'An intimate, fantastical and narrative-driven reflection of Jennifer Lopez''s journey of self-healing and self-love in an immersive world where music and visuals intertwine, revealing the challenges faced and the triumphs achieved.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/nEMSjYpT0B7uxNwu1kEU8fTycs4.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:1217343'),
  ('1053256547080800136', 'This Is My Affair', 1937, 'Romance, Crime, Drama', 'William A. Seiter, Robert H. Planck, Earl Haley', 'Allen Rivkin, Lamar Trotti', 'Robert Taylor, Barbara Stanwyck, Victor McLaglen, Brian Donlevy, John Carradine, Douglas Fowley, Alan Dinehart, Sig Ruman', 'NR', 'President McKinley asks Lt. Richard L. Perry to go underground to identify some obviously very well briefed Mid-Western bank robbers based in Saint Paul, Minnesota.', 'President McKinley asks Lt. Richard L. Perry to go underground to identify some obviously very well briefed Mid-Western bank robbers based in Saint Paul, Minnesota.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/kRP0UHOmWSq6oEx5L1oQjCWxjkp.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:147722'),
  ('753969044892162916', 'This Is My Body', 2001, 'Drama', 'Rodolphe Marconi, Carlo Varini', 'Rodolphe Marconi, Gilles Taurand', 'Louis Garrel, Jane Birkin, Elisabeth Depardieu, Didier Flamand, Annie Girardot, Mélanie Laurent, Didier Bezace, Lila Salet', null, 'Gifted student Antoine goes against his family’s wishes and accepts the lead role in a controversial director’s film. He learns that the role had previously been offered to a young man who committed suicide after an on-set affair – and events conspire to draw Antoine towards the same lover.', 'Gifted student Antoine goes against his family’s wishes and accepts the lead role in a controversial director’s film. He learns that the role had previously been offered to a young man who committed suicide after an on-set affair – and events conspire to draw Antoine towards the same lover.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/zqE3KkR0lj487wrxtS2SxQtCAWn.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:55060'),
